{:edb/db-before-t 667 :edb/db-after-t 668 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533980 50 #inst "2026-10-05T23:44:34.312Z" 13194139533980 true] [17592186087658 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275665 13194139533980 true] [17592186087659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275672 13194139533980 true] [17592186087659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275681 13194139533980 true] [17592186087673 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275658 13194139533980 true] [17592186087673 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275691 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275659 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1089 "q-123773" 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1100 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1113 #uuid "42535d46-cb00-5afc-82ab-e62c0ea06521" 13194139533980 true] [17592186275658 1145 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -1 \\\\ -1 & \\le -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1-1 & \\le 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1+1 \\\\ 0 & \\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+2 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\le 1+2 \\\\ 1 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 3.$" 13194139533980 true] [17592186275659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275660 13194139533980 true] [